e while starting her business.\n  - Gina: Gina owns a clothing store, built a new website, encouraged Jon about his dance studio, and told Jon to \"Just do it!\" after joking about Shia LaBeouf.\n  - stuff: Gina's clothing store has its 'stuff' on display, and Jon congratulated her on how great it looks and the payoff of her hard work.\n  - own business: Gina runs an online clothing store and plans influencer collaborations and ads. Jon runs a dance studio, invests much time, and learns with his successful students.\n  - Gina: Gina advises Jon on marketing, is growing her online store, and asked Jon when he is opening his dance studio. She expressed excitement for his studio opening.\n  - furniture and decor: Gina designed her store space to be cozy and inviting, using furniture that is comfortable and trendy. A chandelier adds a glam feel matching the store's style.\n  - ads: Gina plans to do more ads to reach more people and build her online store's customer base.\n  - clothing store: Gina started an online clothing store; she built a new website for customer orders and got noticed by fashion editors. Jon congratulated her.\n  - Gina: Gina is having some tough times lately, as communicated to Jon, who is supportive.\n  - entrepreneur: Gina and Jon discussed marketing strategies, social media, and influencers. Gina is growing an online store; Jon is promoting his business. They encouraged each other as entrepreneurs.\n  - customers: Gina's customers love her new offers; she focuses on unique pieces. Jon plans to adapt and tweak his business from customer feedback.\n  - customer base: Gina is growing her online store's customer base by launching new offers, promotions, and planning to work with fashion bloggers and influencers for more attention.\n  - Gina: Gina built a new customer ordering website, offered support to Jon about his dance studio struggles, and plans to manage his social media and create content.\n  - Gina: Gina started an online clothing store after