- hobbies: Jolene is seeking tips for balancing hobbies and studies; Deborah focuses on teaching yoga and organizing a yoga event last month.\n  - instrumental tracks with mellow melodies and rhythms: Deborah finds instrumental tracks with mellow melodies and rhythms help create a peaceful vibe for her yoga practice. She likes a track called \"Savana.\"\n  - mindfulness: Jolene realized the importance of mindfulness, self-care, and balance alongside engineering studies after a meditation retreat in Phuket. Deborah encourages this practice.\n  - things that bring you joy: Deborah advises Jolene to make time for 'things that bring you joy' to experience joy.\n  - Nils Frahm: Jolene listens to Nils Frahm for calming music during yoga practice and is seeking recommendations for similar artists.\n  - yoga pose: Jolene's partner performed a yoga pose after a trip to Rio de Janeiro. Jolene asked if the pose helps the partner relax.\n  - yoga on the beach: Jolene expressed interest in trying yoga on the beach and asked if it is a common activity.\n  - meditation course: Jolene signed up for a meditation course at a retreat near a lake, excited to share it with her partner and learn new techniques.\n  - meditation: Jolene uses meditation for self-care, planning a camping trip. She recently tried a new style of meditation with flowers in Thailand.\n  - environment: Jolene aims to devise a more productive and affordable aerial surveillance system for responding to emergencies and monitoring the environment. Deborah noted that environment can enhance practice.\n  - healthy habit: Jolene is thankful for her partner encouraging her goals and is excited to attend a meditation course at a lake retreat. She notes that an easy habit makes a big health difference.\n  - slow down and appreciate the little things: Deborah mentioned life is busy, suggesting they should make an effort to slow down and appreciate the small things, relating it to finding inspiration in small things.\n</ENTI