d assistance regarding children Maria met at a shelter.\n  - John: John set up a 5K charity run to raise funds for veterans and their families and raised awareness and funds against domestic abuse.\n  - John: John joined a service-focused online group last week, felt connected, and shared stories. He participated in events like volunteering at a homeless shelter and organizing a toy drive.\n  - John: John enjoys his new job, finds his team encouraging and inspiring, and is pumped for Maria's next adventure.\n  - John: John joined the fire brigade. He found the training intense but rewarding. He felt their teamwork during their first intense call-out was essential, and his team feels like family.\n  - weight training: John has done weight training, which he found challenging but peaceful, similar to yoga.\n  - John: John joined the fire brigade; the training was intense but rewarding. He recently had his first call-out with his team last Sunday.\n  - John: John had car trouble last Friday on the way to work, causing financial strain. He remains positive and took a road trip last year exploring the coast and national parks in the Pacific Northwest.\n  - John: John joined the fire-fighting brigade, is excited to help the community, and was inspired by the team's dedication and teamwork.\n  - John: John is trying different workout regimes, including considering rock climbing. He acknowledged the importance of staying in shape and expressed belief in the power of supportive people.\n  - John: John acknowledges support is key and appreciates Maria. He finds balance important for well-being. He also made an apple pie for the kids yesterday.\n  - John: John lost his job at a mechanical engineering company and is exploring tech opportunities. He organized a 5K charity run to raise funds for veterans and their families.\n  - John: John joined the fire-fighting brigade to help his community and found the team's dedication and teamwork inspiring, expressing a desire to keep motivating others.\n  - John: John joined the fire-fighting brigade, finding the dedication and teamwork inspiring. He also helped raise canned food, toiletries, and clothes for charity.\n  - picture: Maria commented that a picture was cute and John asked what activities Maria and the subject of the picture enjoy doing together.\n  - events for other causes: Maria asked John if he has done events for other causes after hearing about his 5K charity run for veterans and their families.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2029,"context_chars":8117,"retrieval_duration":0.17375516891479492,"response_duration":2.4995036125183105,"total_duration":2.6732587814331055,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions both hiking and mountaineering, which are the activities listed in the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"COMPLETE","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides all the necessary information to answer the question about the outdoor activities John has done with his colleagues. Specifically, it mentions that John went on a mountaineering trip with workmates and that his colleagues went on a hiking trip. Both activities, hiking and mountaineering, are explicitly stated in the context, matching the elements required in the golden answer.","missing_elements":[],"present_elements":["mountaineering trip with workmates","hiking trip with colleagues"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_4","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_4_qa_130","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What was Tim's huge writing issue last week,as mentioned on November 6, 2023?","golden_answer":"He got stuck on a plot twist","hypothesis":"Tim's huge writing issue last week, as mentioned on November 6, 2023, was that he got stuck on a plot twist. This issue caused him frustration, but he eventually pushed through and got ideas flowing again. The specific date of this writing issue was October 30, 2023.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Tim experienced a major writing issue last week. (event_time: 2023-10-30T00:00:00Z)\n  - Tim experienced a setback while attempting to write a story based on his UK experiences last week. (event_time: 2023-11-14T00:00:00Z)\n  - Tim has been swamped with studies, which occurred in the week prior to 2023-11-21T10:22:00Z. (event_time: 2023-11-14T00:00:00Z)\n  - Tim has been swamped with projects, which occurred in the week prior to 2023-11-21T10:22:00Z. (event_time: 2023-11-14T00:00:00Z)\n  - Tim has been writing more articles recently. (event_time: 2023-08-11T13:08:00Z)\n  - Tim was stuck on a plot twist last week. (event_time: 2023-10-30T00:00:00Z)\n  - The writing issue Tim faced involved being stuck on a plot twist. (event_time: 2023-10-30T00:00:00Z)\n  - Tim is overwhelmed with Assignments this week. (event_time: 2023-08-26T18:59:00Z)\n  - Tim is always taking notes on J.K. Rowling's style for his own writing. (event_time: 2023-10-21T17:51:00Z)\n  - Tim is currently in the middle of writing a fantasy novel. (event_time: 2023-10-21T17:51:00Z)\n  - Tim asks John if anything similar to Tim's struggles with writing has happened with basketball for John. (event_time: 2023-11-21T10:22:00Z)\n  - Writing helps Tim push himself to get better. (event_time: 2023-11-21T10:22:00Z)\n  - her writing really speaks to Tim (event_time: 2023-10-21T17:51:00Z)\n  - Tim is writing articles about fantasy novels. (event_time: 2023-08-02T16:17:00Z)\n  - Tim is writing articles for an online mag. (event_time: 2023-08-02T16:17:00Z)\n  - Tim had a tou