t to express her trans experience, showing her story and helping others understand the trans community.\n  - imperfections: Caroline finds art allows her to explore her transition and changing body, teaching her to accept the beauty of imperfections.\n  - gender identity: Caroline mentioned that creating art, like painting and drawing, was important during her transition to understand and accept her gender identity.\n  - the future: Caroline is excited for the future after taking the first step toward becoming a mom by applying to adoption agencies with help from an advice group.\n  - next time: Melanie asked Caroline what she hopes to do for the next time, following Caroline's volunteering experience.\n  - Caroline: Caroline passed adoption agency interviews last Friday. She is excited to build a family by adopting needy kids, viewing adoption as a way to give back, show love, and acceptance.\n  - my own journey: Caroline shared details of her transgender journey, including struggles and development since coming out and starting transition three years ago, at a school event to inspire others.\n  - Melanie: Melanie congratulated Caroline on passing adoption agency interviews, viewing adoption as a loving way to build a family for needy kids, and encouraged Caroline to be herself.\n  - dad: Caroline used to go horseback riding with her dad through the fields when she was a kid.\n  - body: Caroline mentions that art has allowed her to explore her transition and her changing body, teaching her to accept the beauty of imperfections.\n  - mentors: Caroline is thankful for her mentors' support, which inspires her to keep making art.\n  - counselor: Melanie thinks Caroline would be a great counselor due to her empathy and understanding.\n  - empathy and understanding: Melanie noted that Caroline's empathy and understanding would make her a great counselor, helping people she works with.\n  - books: Caroline appreciates books for guiding, motivating, and helping her discove