lene, where they tried yoga classes.\n  - relationship: Jolene's relationship with her partner was strengthened by discussing loved ones' influence last Friday. Deborah mentioned reconnecting with her mom's friends, bringing up emotional memories.\n  - conversations: Jolene and her partner discussed how loved ones influenced them and their values last Friday. Deborah noted these conversations build relationships.\n  - snake: Jolene has a pet snake she loves dearly; it once escaped and was found under the bed after hours of searching.\n  - Susie: Jolene mentioned that Susie is a great companion. Jolene has had Susie for two years.\n  - Jolene: Jolene attended an awesome yoga retreat where she enjoyed a peaceful setting and an amazing sunrise view. She values catching up with friends like Deborah.\n  - \"It takes two\": \"It takes two\" is a fun, competitive team-strategy game Jolene and another person (implied) enjoy playing together to bond.\n  - Jolene and Anna: Deborah mentioned Anna got her a tasty vegan stir-fry (tofu, veg, ginger, soy sauce). Jolene mentioned doing yoga and meditation last Friday for me-time.\n  - quiet moments: Jolene mentioned that a few quiet moments can work wonders for the soul.\n  - daily routine: Jolene uses breathing, meditation, and yoga for challenges. Deborah meditates, does yoga, and teaches classes in the morning, jogs in a park, and spends evenings with loved ones.\n  - personal time: Jolene schedules personal time as part of her routine to stay balanced and relax, alongside classes and studying.\n  - friends: Jolene had dinner and drinks with her friends the night before last. Jolene mentioned her pals are keeping her company. Deborah attended a music festival with pals and danced.\n  - Jolene's partner's dad: Jolene's partner's dad taught them to stay determined, influencing their partner's creative endeavors.\n  - time for myself: Jolene uses breathing, meditation, and yoga to feel calmer, clearer, more alert, and motivated, an