e last month. It symbolizes her mom's strength and love, holding memories of good and bad times. Deborah's husband was photographed there.\n  - parents: Deborah's parents wed in 1993 and inspired her and her husband. Jolene's parents gave her something at age 10 that started her video game passion. Deborah asked about Jolene's favorite game played with her mom.\n  - Deborah: Deborah enjoyed a music festival, feeling music unites people. She recalls her mother's soothing lullabies and complimented Jolene's tranquil trip photo, highlighting that trips create shared memories.\n  - Jolene and Anna: Deborah mentioned Anna got her a tasty vegan stir-fry (tofu, veg, ginger, soy sauce). Jolene mentioned doing yoga and meditation last Friday for me-time.\n  - Deborah's mother: Deborah's mother enjoyed reading and believed art could give strong emotions and uniquely connect people. Deborah feels close to her mother when visiting art shows.\n  - mother's old house: Deborah visited her mother's old house last Sunday, sitting on a bench to feel her mother's presence. Jolene asked Deborah about special memories regarding her mother at the house.\n  - quote: Deborah received the quote \"Let go of what no longer serves you\" from a friend who is now deceased. Jolene mentioned a quote in her notebook that inspires her to stay focused.\n  - Deborah's mom: Deborah's mom had a big passion for cooking and made amazing meals full of love and warmth that filled the house with wonderful smells.\n  - special symbol: The special symbol represents freedom for Jolene and serves as a reminder to pursue her goals.\n  - birds: Deborah mentioned birds chirping reminded her of what really matters.\n  - Jolene's mom: Jolene's mom cooked with Jolene, which brought everyone together. Jolene asked Deborah about her best memory of cooking with her mom.\n  - quotes: Deborah asked Jolene what other quotes give her strength.\n  - Deborah's mum: Deborah's mum was her biggest fan and source of motivation, often attending Deborah's yoga classes with her.\n  - Simple things: Simple things can indeed bring the most happiness, according to Deborah, who is seeking input on how they have helped Jolene during tough times.\n  - stories about Deborah's mom: Deborah reconnected with her mom's old friends, and hearing stories about her mom was emotional, bringing a mix of happy and sad feelings, but overall comforting.\n  - breeze: Deborah mentioned the gently blowing breeze reminds her of what really matters.\n  - Jolene: Jolene attended an awesome yoga retreat where she enjoyed a peaceful setting and an amazing sunrise view. She values catching up with friends like Deborah.\n  - mom's old friends: Deborah reconnected with her mom's old friends. Hearing their stories was emotional, bringing a mix of happy and sad feelings, but was overall comforting.\n  - certain method: Deborah uses a \"certain method\" to help Jolene figure out what is important and urgent for better organization when overloaded.\n  - paper: Jolene asked Deborah what was written on the paper in a photo.\n  - openness: Openness and love have kept Deborah and family close and happy over the years.\n  - mom's friends: Deborah reconnected with her mom's old friends, which was an emotional experience that brought up both happy and sad feelings, but was overall comforting.\n  - fun: Deborah attended a community meetup last Friday where they shared stories. Deborah asked Jolene what fun events are happening this month.\n  - milestone: Jolene finished a tough engineering project last month, calling it a big milestone she is proud of, having stuck it out despite problems. Deborah congratulated her.\n  - family: Deborah is channeling grief from her father's sudden death two days ago by spending more time with family and cherishing memories, including looking at their 1993 wedding photos.\n  - new poses: Jolene inquired about what new poses Deborah tried after Deborah expressed excitement about a milestone accomplishment.\n  - Something small: Jolene noted that something small can make a real difference and have a big impact.\n</ENTITIES>\n","context_tokens":2096,"context_chars":8344,"retrieval_duration":0.14650964736938477,"response_duration":2.5631656646728516,"total_duration":2.7096753120422363,"grade":true,"grade_reasoning":"The generated answer mentions both Deborah's pendant and Jolene's ring, which aligns with the symbolic gifts referenced in the gold answer.","completeness_grade":"PARTIAL","completeness_reasoning":"The context provides information about Jolene having a pendant that reminds her of her mother, which is relevant to the question. However, it does not explicitly mention that Deborah has a pendant, which is a key element of the golden answer. Therefore, while some relevant information is present, the context is missing the specific detail about Deborah's symbolic gift from her mother, making it incomplete.","missing_elements":["Deborah's pendant"],"present_elements":["Jolene has a pendant that reminds her of her mother"]},{"user_id":null,"graph_id":"v2_full_onto_2_experiment_graph_3","test_id":"v2_full_onto_2_graph_3_qa_144","category":"4","difficulty":"unknown","query":"What kind of impact does Joanna hope to have with her writing?","golden_answer":"share her stories and hopefully have an impact","hypothesis":"Joanna hopes to have a meaningful impact with her writing by making a difference in people's lives. She derives motivation from knowing that her writing can resonate with others, even on tough days. Additionally, she hopes her work gets noticed, particularly her screenplay, and aspires for it to lead to new opportunities and positive feedback. Overall, she believes that meaningful stories come from personal experiences and feelings, and she writes best when being true to herself.","context":"\nFACTS and ENTITIES represent relevant context to the current conversation.\n\n# These are the most relevant facts for the conversation along with the datetime of the event that the fact refers to.\n# If a fact mentions something happening a week ago, then the datetime will be the date time of last week and not the datetime\n# of when the fact was stated.\n# Timestamps in memories represent the actual time the event occurred, not the time the event was mentioned in a message.\n\n<FACTS>\n  - Joanna hopes her work gets noticed. (event_time: 2022-03-18T18:59:00Z)\n  - Joanna intends to continue pursuing her passion for writing. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna derives motivation from knowing her writing can make a difference, even on tough days. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes her screenplay gets noticed and makes it to the screen. (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Writing might be a way for Joanna to find solace. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes for new opportunities stemming from her completed screenplay. (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Writing might be a way for Joanna to express creativity. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna uses writing as a way to express her feelings (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Writing gives Joanna a chance to put down all her thoughts (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna engages in writing. (event_time: 2022-01-21T19:31:00Z)\n  - Joanna views writing as a huge part of who she is. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Writing inspiration helps Joanna stay sharp and motivated. (event_time: 2022-03-24T13:43:00Z)\n  - Joanna believes that she writes meaningful stories best when she is being true to herself (event_time: 2022-05-20T19:49:00Z)\n  - Joanna is a writer. (event_time: 2022-09-14T13:43:00Z)\n  - Nate expressed hope that Joanna's screenplay would do well. (event_time: 2022-06-24T10:55:00Z)\n  - Joanna uses writing to create wild worlds (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Joanna's current writing inspiration involves self-discovery following a loss. (event_time: 2022-02-25T13:07:00Z)\n  - Joanna feels good knowing that people like her writing. (event_time: 2022-08-22T10:57:00Z)\n  - Joanna views writing as an escape mechanism (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Words used in writing have a magical healing effect for Joanna (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna hopes a director will fall in love with her screenplay. (event_time: 2022-02-07T09:27:00Z)\n  - Joanna recently started writing a book. (event_time: 2022-07-10T14:34:00Z)\n  - Joanna explored the theme of love in her writing. (event_time: None)\n  - Joanna uses writing to create awesome characters (event_time: 2022-01-23T14:01:00Z)\n  - Nate is glad that the effects of writing (presumably words) have worked for Joanna. (event_time: 2022-08-14T18:12:00Z)\n  - Joanna feels she cannot stop writing. (event_time: 2022-11-09T17:54:00Z)\n  - Nate encourages Joanna to follow her passion for writing. (event_time: 2022-04-21T19:44:00Z)\n  - Joanna has a strong aptitude for writing. (event_time: 2022-11-07T20:10:00Z)\n  - Joanna explored the theme of sisterhood in her writing. (event_time: None)\n  - Joanna advises practicing writing. (event_time: 2022-03-24T13:43:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - new opportunities: Joanna expressed hope that finishing her first screenplay would lead to new opportunities and positive feedback.\n  - feelings: Writing is a way for Joanna to express her feelings, act as an escape, put thoughts down, and create something good from them, as words have a magical way of healing.\n  - writing projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be the best thing ever, a mix of highs and lows. Writing is an escape, a way to express feelings, and healing.\n  - connection: Joanna is writing a personal story about loss, identity, and connection, which she has had for a long time and is proud to have completed.\n  - literature: Joanna advises reading lots, trying different genres, and writing/sharing literature to build understanding and improve through practice and feedback.\n  - words: Words have a magical way of healing, can turn something sad into something special, and are a significant part of Joanna's writing projects.\n  - meaningful stories: Joanna believes meaningful stories come from personal experiences and feelings, and she writes best when being true to herself, even if difficult.\n  - writing: Joanna feels she cannot stop writing recently, appreciating Nate's support and encouragement.\n  - hope: Joanna experiences a tug-of-war of hope and doubt after wrapping up her second script, feeling a mix of relief and anxiety about future recognition.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - writing inspiration: Joanna uses taking breaks and self-care for writing inspiration to maintain inspiration and mental health, seeking balance.\n  - activities you love: Joanna shared that writing projects are going well, describing the experience as a mix of highs and lows, and that her journal is her rock, viewing writing as a huge part of her life.\n  - feedback: Joanna received positive feedback that people are connecting with her writing, which Nate mentioned.\n  - doubt: Joanna expressed a 'tug-of-war of hope and doubt' after finishing her second script, feeling a mix of excitement and terror about her work getting noticed.\n  - book: Joanna finished writing and editing her book last week, exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams. The book had previously been shared with her writers group.\n  - \"Finding Home\": \"Finding Home\" is a script Joanna is writing with her writers group about a girl's journey to find her true home. She finds the work rewarding and emotional.\n  - dialogue: Joanna found it rewarding to see the dialogue she wrote acted out, noting it was the third time this happened. Seeing characters and dialogue from her writing performed was an amazing experience.\n  - Joanna: Joanna is filming her own movie based on her road-trip script. She finds every day on set awesome and is excited to show her vision.\n  - journal: Joanna uses her journal as her rock while she is busy with writing projects, finding it helps her express feelings and heal.\n  - movie script: Joanna is filming a movie based on her road-trip script. She previously hoped for big-screen distribution, and Nate asked about future script submissions.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - sisterhood: Joanna watched a story exploring themes of sisterhood, love, and chasing dreams, which she recommended. She also finished writing her book last week after many late nights and edits.\n  - dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness: Joanna mentioned a page with dialogues exploring loss, redemption, and forgiveness for her next movie; she finds the story deep and emotional.\n  - Jo: Joanna (Jo) asked Nate if he celebrated good feedback people are connecting with his writing. Previously, she asked about a couple he met while walking Max.\n  - passion: Joanna's writing is a huge part of her; Nate turned his passion for gaming into a career by winning an international tournament.\n  - writing gig: Joanna had an audition yesterday for a writing gig, feeling a mix of excitement and anxiety afterward. Nate previously encouraged her, noting her hard work and passion.\n  - old notebooks: Joanna found old notebooks containing her early writings last week, showing her progress. Nate asked Joanna what she was working on in that notebook.\n  - inspiring quotes: Joanna's cork board is filled with inspiring quotes and pictures for motivation and creativity.\n  - bookmark: Joanna finished a cute little bookmark for a lady at her 